the cable render needs performance work. the connections take a while to apply, it should also be possible to grab a cable from a connection and connect it somewhere else.
   -> DONE. Renderer was NOT slow (0.05ms); the 3s xrandr-cache round trip was (274ms cold). Now prewarmed. Re-grab added.

the config generator missbehaves. its keeping a stale pgm and prv channels that are not used anyway and not visible in the gui.
it also doesnt react when i changed connected destination from pgm 2 to multiview for decklink output 3 but after many restarts it still displays pgm2.
   -> DONE. Both: phantom channels from cabling multiview/stream, and your config had TWO decklink entries on device 3.


editing screen destinations custom resolution acts weird. setting width is normal, then i try to set height and it defaults back to 1080, after a second time it changes to desired in a screen dest node, but stays 1080 in the inspector.
this is probably linked to the stale ch1&2.
   -> DONE. NOT linked to the stale channels - it was a 5s client cache answering the read after your save.

the operator gui firefox fails to open on the selected monitor. but the mouse is locked to the correct monitor.
the xrandr workflow needs a review. after manualy running DISPLAY=:0 xdotool search --onlyvisible --name "Mozilla Fir
efox" windowmove 3072 0 it showed correct and restarts correct.
   -> DONE. xdotool searched the wrong WM_CLASS field so it never matched and burned an 8s timeout. Now verified+retried.

